  "reviewer_source_findings": {
    "adaptation": "Exact supplied reviewer diff was compared with the named accepted after254 reviewer. Changes pin the after260 next6 collector SHA, ROOT260 acceptance/publication hashes and counts, the six listed targets, intake schema and diagnostic labels. The reviewer fixes the previously identified audit-path canonicalization by requiring the exact final audit path and SHA as CLI inputs, canonicalizing the path under the fixed root, and binding it to the intake's sole audit reference.",
    "collector_boundary": "Reviewer hash-checks the pinned after260 next6 finite-record collector, loads it in a non-main namespace, and calls its in-memory propose gate. It explicitly reports shared finite gate reuse rather than claiming an independent duplicate implementation of every collector gate.",
    "strict_source_and_runtime_gates": "The reviewed collector source requires exactly the six strict producer refs, PASS plus integer exit zero, no guard error, the configured memory guard, source/pin/compiler/runtime before-after bindings, exact command and output/cwd provenance, explicit current target/direct-supplier source and object providers, exact present object-slot sets, and matching direct dependency/source/object maps. The reviewer separately requires the six final target source hashes and six supplied strict PASS statuses.",
    "stock_and_complete_all_gates": "The reviewed collector requires one completed original audit that covers exactly the six targets, the complete named sidecar set with SHA bindings, audit PASS and stable inputs, matching strict sources/objects/pins/tools/runner/template, one successful complete inventory/type/axiom stage, one stock replay per target with actual command and log bindings, and exact declaration JSON/log/inventory equality. The reviewer checks one ALL stage and six stock stages and requires module record counts to match the proposal.",
    "record_and_type_gates": "The reviewer requires proposed census and declaration rows to equal recomputation; exact append-only six-module set; old 260 census entries and 8296 records deeply equal; nonempty records for every new target; artifact-derived totals and per-module deltas; unique identities and no fullname collision; complete nonempty types without ellipsis; unsafe, partial and axiom flags false; and axioms contained in {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}.",
    "current_sources_and_objects": "The reviewer rehashes every owned source and every currently present owned object slot over the 260 accepted modules plus six targets. Target/current provider references and exact slot sets are bound through intake; the fixed slots cover .olean, .olean.private, .olean.server, .ilean and .ir. This is finite current-object checking, not ancestry or import-closure replay.",
    "status_and_claim_scope": "Successful result remains FINITE_RECORD_STAGE_TERMINAL_REVIEW_PASS_NOT_ROOT_ACCEPTANCE with proof_credit 0, root_acceptance null, main status OPEN, and explicit false external/project closure replay claims. Errors become BLOCKED with nonzero reviewer exit. No future audit result or PASS is predicted by this CP.",
    "scope_limit": "The reviewer uses the collector's finite proposal gate and normal imported-environment trust. It does not independently replay every gate, invoke a compiler/checker, prove unconditional main, or replay full project/import/external closure."
  },
